⍝ csubrow.apls -- Dyalog APL, one row at a time (2026): an explicit :For
⍝ over iy, with each row written as a single vector expression. The
⍝ halfway house between csubraw.apls (element loop) and csubary.apls (one
⍝ array expression), like the "vectors" variants in Python, PDL and C.
⍝ The input is offset by 0.5 so it stays floating point. Run as
⍝    dyalogscript csubrow.apls 1000 2000 10
⎕IO←0
∇ out←csub(in nx ny out);iy
  :For iy :In ⍳ny
      out[iy;]←in[iy;]+iy+⍳nx
  :EndFor
∇
args←2⎕NQ#'GetCommandLineArgs'
(nrpt nx ny)←⍎¨¯3↑(1↓args),(0⌈4-≢args)↑'1000' '2000' '10'
in←0.5+(nx+ny)-(⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx
out←ny nx⍴0.5
⎕←'Arrays ',(⍕nx),' by ',(⍕ny),' count ',⍕nrpt
:For r :In ⍳nrpt
    out←csub in nx ny out
:EndFor
:If ∨/,out≠in+(⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx
    ⎕←'Error: result does not match'
:EndIf
